From: kuncy7 <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: add the missing rx_desc_get_offset to ipq5018_ops

Selecting the 512MB ath11k memory profile panics every IPQ5018 board at
radio bring-up:

  Unable to handle kernel execute from non-executable memory at 0000000000000000
  pc : 0x0
  lr : ath11k_dp_rx_pdev_alloc+0x5c8/0x680 [ath11k]

207-ath11k-Enable-256_512MB-profiles.patch compiles an extra call into
ath11k_dp_rxdma_ring_sel_config() under CPTCFG_ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_512M:

  static void ath11k_dp_get_rx_header_offset(...)
  {
	ab->hw_params.hw_ops->rx_desc_get_offset(tlv_filter);
  }

The call is unconditional, but the op was only filled in for ipq8074_ops,
ipq6018_ops, qca6390_ops and qcn9074_ops. ipq5018_ops does not have it,
so the call goes to NULL. Without the 512M profile the whole function is
a "return 0" stub, which is why the default (1GB) build never sees this.

ipq5018_ops is used by both ATH11K_HW_IPQ5018_HW10 and
ATH11K_HW_QCN6122_HW10, so on a 512M build every radio on the SoC dies;
only a PCIe QCN9074 survives, because qcn9074_ops has the pointer.

Use the qcn9074 variant: every other rx_desc accessor in ipq5018_ops is
the qcn9074 one, i.e. the descriptor really is struct hal_rx_desc_qcn9074.
The op, its helpers and the other tables' entries all live inside the
same #ifdef, so this is inert unless the 512M profile is selected.

Reported-by: zmu (Redmi AX5400), georgem83 (Linksys MX2000)
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.c
@@ -1483,6 +1483,9 @@
 	.rx_desc_mpdu_start_addr2 = ath11k_hw_ipq9074_rx_desc_mpdu_start_addr2,
 	.get_ring_selector = ath11k_hw_ipq8074_get_tcl_ring_selector,
 	.rx_desc_get_hal_mpdu_len = ath11k_hw_qcn9074_rx_desc_get_hal_mpdu_len,
+#ifdef CPTCFG_ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_512M
+	.rx_desc_get_offset = ath11k_hw_qcn9074_rx_desc_get_offset,
+#endif
 };
 
 #define ATH11K_TX_RING_MASK_0 BIT(0)
